# Residential HTTP proxy profile - merge after .env.tgweb.example
#
# Usage:
#   cat config/env/.env.residential.example >> .env
#   # set PARSER_PROXY_LIST with real provider credentials
#   make proxy-check && make preflight-tgweb && make tgweb-crawl-residential
#
# Requires: paid residential proxy (DataImpulse, IPRoyal, ...). Not VPS Squid.
# Prefer sticky session per provider (same exit IP for crawl batch).
# Preflight checks proxy username for country/session tokens.
# Do not use placeholder URLs - crawl hard-fails on first fetch.
#
# Docs: docs/OPS.md#proxy

# One provider (pay-as-you-go ~$1-7/GB). Comma-separate for rotation + CF cooldown.
# PARSER_PROXY_LIST=http://YOUR_USER:YOUR_PASS@gw.dataimpulse.com:823
# PARSER_PROXY_LIST=http://YOUR_USER:YOUR_PASS@geo.iproyal.com:12321

# Session / geo targeting is usually encoded in the username (see provider dashboard):
# PARSER_PROXY_LIST=http://user-country-us-session-abc:pass@host:port
